{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02483",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 4.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.93,
      "end_seconds": 15.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.82,
      "end_seconds": 21.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "It's burning pain in the upper tummy, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.17,
      "end_seconds": 26.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "So, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.79,
      "end_seconds": 31.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Probably about four days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.44,
      "end_seconds": 43.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.01,
      "end_seconds": 58.89,
      "duration_seconds": 12.88,
      "text": "I, I get some relief from antacids. It's on and off. Erm, I've also been feeling full quickly. Oh, and indigestion. Had that since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.87,
      "end_seconds": 63.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.82,
      "end_seconds": 66.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.65,
      "end_seconds": 74.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.17,
      "end_seconds": 96.13,
      "duration_seconds": 20.96,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.84,
      "end_seconds": 101.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.63,
      "end_seconds": 105.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Paracetamol, 650 milligrams, maybe, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.17,
      "end_seconds": 110.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.86,
      "end_seconds": 137.24,
      "duration_seconds": 26.38,
      "text": "Right, no, it's at home. I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. Well, I take Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. Sorry, what was I saying, I take ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 138.62,
      "end_seconds": 144.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 200 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.75,
      "end_seconds": 149.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.29,
      "end_seconds": 155.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Uh, um, no, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.46,
      "end_seconds": 164.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.68,
      "end_seconds": 168.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Okay, so my son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.48,
      "end_seconds": 187.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.79,
      "end_seconds": 200.65,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, yes, naproxen. I get a rash. Ah, yes, trimethoprim, it gives me itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.24,
      "end_seconds": 204.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.25,
      "end_seconds": 214.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "I've got arthritis in my knees. I have an enlarged prostate, for about a year. I have COPD."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.18,
      "end_seconds": 222.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Okay, I can see COPD in your file as well. Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.48,
      "end_seconds": 228.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.53,
      "end_seconds": 249.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "And what about weight loss, vomiting blood, difficulty swallowing or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.82,
      "end_seconds": 253.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.05,
      "end_seconds": 257.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.12,
      "end_seconds": 261.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "So, no, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.83,
      "end_seconds": 266.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.14,
      "end_seconds": 270.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Yeah, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 272.05,
      "end_seconds": 277.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 81, pressure 113 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.06,
      "end_seconds": 280.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.41,
      "end_seconds": 284.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.36,
      "end_seconds": 288.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.47,
      "end_seconds": 304.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Your upper tummy is tender in the middle with no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.1,
      "end_seconds": 325.38,
      "duration_seconds": 16.28,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Having listened and examined, it points towards a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Reflux is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.96,
      "end_seconds": 332.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Hmm, is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.81,
      "end_seconds": 343.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.3,
      "end_seconds": 363.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood count for dyspepsia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.75,
      "end_seconds": 366.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.74,
      "end_seconds": 404.09,
      "duration_seconds": 33.35,
      "text": "I think a stool test for helicobacter makes sense here, for dyspepsia. I'm prescribing omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, eight weeks. That's for stomach ulcer. Stop the ibuprofen and use paracetamol for the knee pain instead. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's review you in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.88,
      "end_seconds": 408.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.32,
      "end_seconds": 412.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.96,
      "end_seconds": 416.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}